    "background_story": "Marie was a delicate monarch butterfly with wings of iridescent beauty. Her life began as a tiny egg on a milkweed leaf, and she spent her early days fluttering around the warm sunlight. As she grew, Marie's wings developed a stunning pattern of orange and black, with delicate veins that shimmered like glass. She spent her days flitting from flower to flower, sipping nectar and spreading pollen. But Marie's most remarkable trait was her migratory journey. Every year, she would join millions of monarchs on an epic flutter across continents, braving winds and storms to reach their wintering grounds. Marie's determination and resilience inspired generations of butterflies, and her story became a legend among the insect kingdom.",
